Be sure to get all the seeds here, then talk to the mayor inside the northwest house; he'll tell you to leave, but the Goddess herself will come and speak up for us once we try to leave.  Afterwards, follow Nevan, your new party member, into the Ship, and watch as it heads off for the Island of Murdaw!

Ashlynn herself will then ask to stay behind, but that's ok; we can only have four party members anyway, and we can still use her outside of Murdaw's Dungeon.  Before going in, equip your party like so.  If you didn't remember to keep the Bronze Shield and Hardwood Headware, never fear.  Nevan's durability isn't all that important anyway, not for the upcoming fights.  In any case, head on in...

== Murdaw's Keep: Part 1 (1st Visit) ==

[[File:DQ6 Murdaw's Keep Part 1.png|thumb]]

This will not be the last time this guide will guide you to this place.  The Chain Whip, Seed of Life, 1150G, and Full Plate Armour are all kind of off the beaten path, and we have another Seed of Life to get from Wellshire anyway.  So, run from everyone, get the Chain Whip and Seed of Life, use Evac, get the 1150G and Full Plate Armour (equip on Nevan), then use Evac.  Do that, and you'll be done with it for now.  So head on over to Wellshire!

{{sidebar|title=Important Note for SNES players!|width=400px|float=left|contents=Now is when SNES players should should be able to buy the Enchanted Armour.  Ashlynn's going to be replaced by a fourth party member very shortly, one who will need nothing from you but a Bronze Shield and some Hardwood Headware; so sell all of her stuff except for the Gold Bracer and Bunny Ears.  Then sell everything Milly has except for the Agility Ring, and sell whatever other outdated gear you need to!  And no, you will not need the Thorn Whips; they will be replaced by better weapons later.}}
{{-|left}}

== Wellshire ==

Go to the house in the Northeast corner, and you will find the mayor in a state of panic; his daughter has been kidnapped!  Talk to him again, and he will leave to rescue her.  You, however, are more than capable of doing that task for him, so head northeast to the well!  Once you do, talk to the thug, say '''Yes''', and then say '''No''' to trigger a fight!

