There's really no advice to give other than you should kill Liddle first, and wait until he's dead before trying to Sap Bigg (Selflessness will tank status moves as well).  These guys are joke bosses; their whole shtick is that they are the Team Rocket of this game.  Kick their butts, and once you do, the mayor will show up.  Some dialogue prompts will come up, and you will have two choices as to what you can say.  

<blockquote>
Say '''Yes''', and you will receive 5000G for your dishonesty

Say '''No''', and drop by his house later on to receive a Seed of Life.
</blockquote>

For the purposes of beating Murdaw as reliably as possible, you are recommended to fight these guys, then choose the second option.  However, you can also choose to just give them the 5000G, at which point you will be faced with the following options instead.

<blockquote>
Say '''Yes''', and you will receive 5000G as compensation (so basically, you neither gain or lose anything from this sidequest).

Say '''No''', and drop by his house later on to receive a Seed of Life and a Prayer Ring (restores 30 MP, and can be used multiple times.  Be warned though, it has a random chance of disappearing after every use).
</blockquote>

The Prayer Ring is somewhat nifty, but it's not worth losing 5000G (and therefore, the Enchanted Armour) over.  After all, you should still have at least one Magic Water on you, and you're going to get another one from the 1st Half of Murdaw's Keep.  Speaking of which, head on back over there; because this time, you're not stopping till you get to the big man himself!  Before you go to face him, make sure your party is equipped as thus...

